WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.293 --> 00:00:04.880
Any time you combine
spirituality and capitalism,

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:07.049
it has the potential to go really dark.

00:00:08.091 --> 00:00:10.427
We look at the success,
we look at the failure,

00:00:10.511 --> 00:00:12.554
we look at the ambition,
we look at the heartbreak.

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:14.306
-We!
-Work!

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:15.641
Everybody scream!

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.980
WeCrashed is our take on the story of

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:23.315
Adam and Rebekah
Neumann.

00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:26.068
We meet Adam and Rebekah
when they are

00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:27.277
kind of at the beginning

00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:29.863
of building a company
about building dreams.

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:31.782
In her mind, it's more than
a shared workspace.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:35.202
It's a profound idea
about how to connect all of humanity.

00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.454
And she just knew
that they could change the world.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:39.873
We're selling an experience...

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:41.542
a community.

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:45.337
Adam's really passionate,
and he was a great salesman,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.214
but he also failed a lot.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:50.759
They were both struggling
to survive in New York City,

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:53.512
two struggling people
who happened to find gold.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:55.097
You have to make them see.

00:00:55.472 --> 00:00:56.515
See what?

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:57.599
You're a supernova.

00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.226
They're crazy in love,

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.895
so the heights
that they achieved in their life

00:01:01.979 --> 00:01:04.064
were absolutely
fueled by their connection,

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:07.359
which also meant that the lows
were fueled by their connection.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:09.820
They build something remarkable

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.613
with billions of dollars in revenue.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.532
You were supposed to be
getting us funding.

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:15.367
But now you're telling us
to spend more?

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.328
Miguel, we spend to grow.

00:01:18.412 --> 00:01:19.872
And you see how

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:22.541
money and power
starts infecting them.

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:24.877
There's late nights,
there's sleep deprivation,

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.044
there's a lot of drinking,

00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:28.255
kind of really blurring the lines
between work and personal.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.133
I say, "We!"
You say, "Work!"

00:01:31.216 --> 00:01:33.260
-We!
-Work!

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.182
It's fascinating that
really smart,

00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:39.641
hard-working people

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:42.227
can be swept up
and intoxicated by power.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:43.353
You think you built this?

00:01:43.437 --> 00:01:44.771
I built this!

00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:48.150
We've gotten to see

00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:50.110
Adam and Rebekah's
public face,

00:01:50.194 --> 00:01:53.197
but this... our hope is
you'll truly feel like you're getting

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:57.034
a behind-the-scenes glimpse
of what's played out on the front pages.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.494
I think the thing
that makes WeCrashed unique

00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:00.913
is we are living in a moment

00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:05.292
where there is this very real push
to be billionaires.

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:09.296
And this show looks at
the potential cost of that.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:11.465
We made a choice
not to villainize them.

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:13.008
The media's already done that.

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:15.260
And the true story
is so much more complicated,

00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:16.470
and it's so much more interesting.

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:21.266
Let's show you who these people are
and let you into their personal journey.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.560
I just can't be nothing again.

00:02:23.644 --> 00:02:25.479
You'll never be nothing.

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:28.815
I want you to meet
the legendary Adam Neumann.

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:31.235
To have these Oscar-winning actors
at the center of it,

00:02:31.318 --> 00:02:32.402
it's really special.

00:02:32.486 --> 00:02:35.739
Annie Hathaway is simply one of the best.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.699
Annie is just perfect.

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:40.327
I've genuinely never had
an experience like this before.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.163
It was an amazing part
to really get to sink my teeth into.

00:02:43.247 --> 00:02:46.083
You took everything I believe in!

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:48.544
I think Jared playing Adam,
he's magnetic.

00:02:48.627 --> 00:02:49.795
You can't take your eyes off of him.

00:02:50.337 --> 00:02:53.131
-Are you with me?
-Yes!

00:02:53.215 --> 00:02:56.844
It's an epic rise and fall story
like you've never seen before.

00:02:56.927 --> 00:02:58.679
In some way,
this is an aspirational story.

00:02:58.762 --> 00:03:00.597
In some ways, it's a cautionary tale.

00:03:00.681 --> 00:03:01.723
I love this series.

00:03:01.807 --> 00:03:03.767
I really enjoyed that challenge,

00:03:03.851 --> 00:03:05.602
to play a bigger-than-life
person like this.

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.771
It's, in every way, fun.

00:03:07.855 --> 00:03:09.398
And it's exciting,
it's adventurous,

00:03:09.481 --> 00:03:11.733
it's hilarious,
and it's very touching.

00:03:12.651 --> 00:03:14.319
We're doing something different.

00:03:14.403 --> 00:03:16.780
We're building a community.

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:20.742
We do this together,
we can change everything.

